The same three scores can give different decisions when the cutoff changes.

```javascript
const scores = [0.4, 0.6, 0.8];
function countPositive(threshold) {
  return scores.filter(score => score >= threshold).length;
}
console.log(countPositive(0.5));
console.log(countPositive(0.7));
```

It prints 2, then 1. Raising the threshold leaves fewer scores counted as positive.
